From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:06:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on the Dell Latitude 5455

The Latitude 5455 shares the Latitude 7455's board and firmware, and the
7455 is already on the list. Without QSEECOM the laptop has no EFI
variables, so an installer cannot write its boot entry.
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 4d47cad..7c2d91d 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2308,6 +2308,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a16-ux3607oa" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,inspiron-14-plus-7441" },
+	{ .compatible = "dell,latitude-5455" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,latitude-7455" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,xps13-9345" },
 	{ .compatible = "ecs,liva-qc710" },
-- 
2.56.0

